# task t2 (reproducibility): the headline-metric evidence file used to live OUTSIDE
# version control (models/fix_metrics.json was generated, git-ignored and never
# archived). Its in-repo stand-in, and the external-corpus provenance manifest that
# makes the 1561-image training corpus traceable, are archived here instead.
!reports/fix_metrics_restored.json
!reports/external_corpus_manifest.json
# task t2 (evidence-worker): a FRESH end-to-end run of the default entry point
# (`python scripts/smoke_test.py`) on 2026-10-12. The archived reports/smoke_test.json
# is deliberately left as the file docs/results.md §5 was written from; this is the
# re-measurement (P50 1679 / P95 2406 ms, same frozen decision TP56/TN63/FP0/FN0).
!reports/smoke_test_fresh_run.json
# improvement round (work/improvement-plan.md): the pre-improvement baseline, the
# pre-registered gate evaluation and its NEGATIVE-result write-up, the review-band
# tuning grid, the adaptive-localisation output, and the source-controlled video
# validation. These ARE the evidence for the improvement claims, so they must be in
# version control -- leaving them ignored would reproduce exactly the defect that
# lost models/fix_metrics.json.
!reports/baseline_improvement.json
!reports/decision_gate_validation.json
!reports/decision_gate_negative_result.json
!reports/review_band_tuning.json
!reports/localization_regions.json
!reports/video_temporal_validation.json
!reports/operating_point_analysis.json
# These four files REFUTE the published "real claim photos: FPR 0% (0/41)" claim:
# they measure the frozen deployment heads on those same 41 web-sourced real photos and
# get FPR 92.68% (38/41). They must be in version control -- a refutation that is
# gitignored is not a refutation. See work/audit/audit-1.md D2.
!reports/testset_real_41_eval.md
!reports/testset_real_41_diagnosis.json
!reports/testset_real_41_integrity.json
!reports/testset_real_41_reprocessing.json

